* 2N3904 NPN BJT model card — Lab 04 CE voltage-divider SPICE reference
*
* Origin: the widely published ON Semiconductor / Motorola 2N3904 SPICE model
* card (also distributed in the PSpice Evaluation library). No Instructor
* Starter Kit was provided for ENG29 2121, so this public model card is used
* instead of an institution-specific file.
*
* Cross-checked on 2026-11-24 against:
*   https://ece.mcgill.ca/~grober4/SPICE/SPICE_Decks/1st_Edition/chapter8/fig8_24.cir
*   https://home.uncg.edu/~ehhellen/spice_stuff.html
*   https://github.com/fakuivan/ltspice-models/blob/master/2N3904.lib
*
* Parameters copied verbatim; do not tune to match analytical results.
* Changing a parameter here changes every SPICE run and must be recorded in
* docs/validation.md together with the new SHA256 of this file.
*
* Parameter names are upper-case for readability; SPICE model parameter names
* are case-insensitive.
.model Q2N3904 NPN (IS=6.734f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259
+ ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5 BR=.7371 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1
+ CJC=3.638p MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=.2593 VJE=.75
+ TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)
